/*!

@mainpage Lakehouse API C++ Client Library

An idiomatic C++ client library for the [Lakehouse API][cloud-service-docs].

The Lakehouse API (formerly BigLake API) provides access to a serverless,
fully managed, and highly available metastore that provides a single
source of truth for your data lakehouse. It lets multiple
engines—including Apache Spark, Google Managed Spark, Apache Flink, Trino
and BigQuery—share tables and metadata for key open formats (Apache
Iceberg, Apache Hive), and query the same copy of data. Plus, through the
Lakehouse runtime catalog federation seamlessly unite your lakehouse
ecosystem, letting Iceberg compatible engines on Google Cloud (BigQuery,
Google Managed Spark) discover and analyze enterprise data across
Snowflake, Databricks, and AWS Glue.

While this library is **GA**, please note that the Google Cloud C++ client libraries do **not** follow
[Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).

@tableofcontents{HTML:2}

## Quickstart

The following shows the code that you'll run in the
`google/cloud/biglake/quickstart/` directory,
which should give you a taste of the Lakehouse API C++ client library API.

@snippet quickstart.cc all

## Main classes

<!-- inject-client-list-start -->
The main class in this library is
[`biglake_hive_v1::HiveMetastoreServiceClient`](@ref google::cloud::biglake_hive_v1::HiveMetastoreServiceClient). All RPCs are exposed
as member functions of this class. Other classes provide helpers, configuration
parameters, and infrastructure to mock
[`biglake_hive_v1::HiveMetastoreServiceClient`](@ref google::cloud::biglake_hive_v1::HiveMetastoreServiceClient) when testing your
application.
<!-- inject-client-list-end -->

## More Information

- @ref common-error-handling - describes how the library reports errors.
- @ref biglake-override-endpoint - describes how to override the default
  endpoint.
- @ref biglake-override-authentication - describes how to change the
  authentication credentials used by the library.
- @ref biglake-override-retry - describes how to change the default retry
  policies.
- @ref biglake-env - describes environment variables that can configure the
  behavior of the library.
- @ref biglake-override-universe-domain - describes how to override the default universe domain.

[cloud-service-docs]: https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/iceberg-tables#create-using-biglake-metastore

*/
